        "howNativesThink": "Native finance professionals treat a 'benchmark' as the indispensable comparative anchor: an absolute return percentage (e.g., 9%) is fundamentally meaningless until measured against its relevant benchmark index (e.g., if the benchmark gained 15%, the fund underperformed by 600 basis points). Instinctively, native speakers associate 'benchmark' with rigor, transparency, and fiduciary accountability\u2014beating the benchmark justifies active management fees (alpha), while trailing it signals underperformance.",
        "mentalImage": "A portfolio manager in front of a dual-screen Bloomberg terminal pointing at a comparative line graph, tracking the upward trajectory of a high-yield tech fund against the dashed white baseline of the benchmark S&P 500 Index.",
