        "howNativesThink": "To a native finance professional, 'contribution' has two primary resonances depending on context: profitability analysis and compensation benefits. When reviewing a product line or business unit, an accountant does not merely look at net profit; they look at 'contribution margin'\u2014asking whether a product covers its variable costs and leaves enough to help pay for the building and executive salaries. When speaking with HR or personal finance advisors, natives immediately associate 'contribution' with their retirement wealth: 'What percentage is your 401(k) contribution, and does the company match it?' They view employee contributions as disciplined long-term wealth building, while employer matching is seen as 'free money'.",
