        "howNativesThink": "While everyday consumers might initially assume that falling prices sound wonderful ('everything is getting cheaper!'), native economists and financial professionals regard deflation as one of the most perilous macroeconomic threats\u2014far more insidious and difficult to reverse than moderate inflation. They recognize that if prices decline continuously, consumers stop buying cars, houses, and electronics today because they expect them to be cheaper next quarter. Businesses cannot maintain margins, so they freeze hiring, cut wages, and default on fixed loans whose nominal repayment amounts never decrease. Natives instinctively associate deflation with stagnation, negative benchmark interest rates, and central bank intervention.",
