        "howNativesThink": "To corporate strategists and business leaders, economies of scale represent the foundational economic logic behind mergers, automated mega-factories, and global supply chains: 'the more you make, the cheaper each unit becomes'. If an automated vehicle assembly plant costs one billion dollars to construct, producing ten thousand cars incurs an unsustainable fixed cost of one hundred thousand dollars per car, but producing one million cars reduces that fixed burden to one thousand dollars per car. Executives associate this concept with bulk purchasing power, operating leverage, and formidable barriers to entry that protect incumbents against smaller rivals.",
