        "howNativesThink": "To native business executives and consumers, insurance is an indispensable risk-management shield rather than a discretionary expense. Natives instinctively conceptualize insurance through four interconnected mechanics: the 'policy' (the governing legal contract), the 'premium' (the recurring subscription fee paid to maintain coverage), the 'deductible' (the out-of-pocket threshold absorbed before the insurer pays), and the 'claim' (the formal assertion of a covered loss). In idiomatic corporate speech, 'an insurance policy' is also deployed metaphorically to denote any deliberate redundancy or hedging strategy designed to prevent operational catastrophe.",
