        "howNativesThink": "To native speakers, 'profit' represents the fundamental metric of enterprise viability: it is what remains after the hard costs of reality are paid. Natives intuitively picture a ledger moving 'into the black' (away from 'in the red'), symbolizing a business that generates more value than it consumes. Beyond finance, native speakers employ 'profit' metaphorically in formal register to signify any practical benefit or wisdom harvested from experience, but in contemporary corporate contexts, it evokes the relentless pursuit of healthy margins and quarterly earnings per share.",
        "mentalImage": "A corporate income statement displayed on an analyst dual-screen workstation, highlighting the bolded bottom row labeled 'Net Profit After Tax,' showing positive double-digit percentage growth in crisp green figures beside a fountain pen and a newly compiled quarterly earnings summary.",
