        "howNativesThink": "To native speakers, 'prudence' is a dignified, reassuring quality associated with financial maturity, seasoned stewardship, and long-term sustainability. It is the polar opposite of reckless speculation, rash impulse, or hype-driven gambles. In executive communication, phrases like 'fiscal prudence' or 'an abundance of prudence' signal to investors and stakeholders that management is protecting the core business from downside risk rather than gambling shareholder capital. In banking and accounting, prudence provides the philosophical justification for keeping healthy cash buffers and writing down impaired assets promptly.",
