        "evolution": "Originally a 15th-century military term describing the regrouping of scattered troops after being driven back in combat ('rally the troops'). In the 1880s, the term was adopted by stock exchange traders and financial journalists on Wall Street and the London Stock Exchange to describe a sudden, robust rebound in stock or commodity prices following a sharp sell-off or protracted bear market. Today, it denotes any marked upward price movement in equity, bond, or currency markets, whether brief ('bear market rally', 'relief rally') or sustained ('year-end rally', 'Santa Claus rally').",
