        "howNativesThink": "To a native speaker in business and finance, 'rally' instantly triggers an image of green candlestick charts surging upward after a nerve-racking drop. It conveys active resurgence\u2014buyers stepping in en masse to bid up prices because sentiment has decisively flipped from panic to opportunistic buying. Native speakers distinguish a 'rally' (dynamic upward surge following a drop) from simple steady growth ('steady increase') or a speculative bubble.",
