        "commonMistakes": "Learners often misplace stress onto the initial syllable of 'return' (*REE-turn*) or over-emphasize the preposition (*return ON investment*). When pronouncing the acronym 'ROI', non-native speakers occasionally attempt to read it as an unseparated phonetic word (*roy*) instead of reciting the individual letters /\u02cc\u0251\u02d0r.o\u028a\u02c8a\u026a/. Conceptually, learners frequently confuse 'return on investment' (a percentage ratio measuring net profitability relative to capital expenditure: Net Income / Capital Invested \u00d7 100) with 'operating margin' (operating profit divided by net sales) or 'absolute profit' (gross cash generated). Furthermore, non-native speakers often overlook that simple ROI fails to reflect the time horizon of cash flows, necessitating annualized ROI or Internal Rate of Return (IRR) for accurate multi-year comparisons.",
        "ipa": "/r\u026a\u02c8t\u025c\u02d0rn \u0251\u02d0n \u026an\u02c8v\u025bst.m\u0259nt/",
