        "howNativesThink": "To a native English speaker in business, 'return on investment' (and its acronym 'ROI') serves as the ultimate litmus test for credibility and resource justification. Whether pitching a $5 million enterprise IT overhaul or requesting a $200 software subscription, the immediate instinctive inquiry is: 'What's the ROI?' Culturally, native speakers extend the concept beyond balance sheets into everyday professional productivity, evaluating the 'ROI on my time' or 'ROI on networking'. Proposing any initiative without demonstrating a tangible, defensible return on investment is perceived as unprofessional, speculative, or undisciplined.",
