        "howNativesThink": "To native business professionals and consumers, hearing that an expenditure is tax deductible is an immediate psychological trigger that reduces the perceived cost of the expense. However, native accountants caution against the classic amateur fallacy that tax deductible means free. Natives understand that if a company in a 25% tax bracket spends $1,000 on a tax-deductible conference, it does not get $1,000 back from the government; rather, its taxable income is reduced by $1,000, saving $250 in taxes while still incurring a net cash outflow of $750. In non-profit culture, charitable organizations constantly highlight their 501(c)(3) tax-deductible status to incentivize corporate sponsorships and private endowments.",
